**Definition GAW7.** For a prime $q>5$ and an even integer $k\ge2$, let
$A_k(q)$ mean that $p=kq+1$ is prime and $\rho(p)\mid\pi(q)$. Put

$$
\begin{aligned}
A_{\{2\}}(q)&:=A_2(q),\\
A_{[4,200]}(q)&:\Longleftrightarrow
  \exists k\in[4,200],\ k\text{ even},\ A_k(q),\\
A_{>200}(q)&:\Longleftrightarrow
  \exists k>200,\ k\text{ even},\ A_k(q).
\end{aligned}                                                    \tag{GAW7}
$$

Let $E_{200}$ denote the assertion that
$A_{[4,200]}(q)$ is false for every prime $q>5$.

